memslots-before-vcpus

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Register memslots before vCPUs to skip KVM's SRCU wait on restore. Backport of upstream PR 6388 (commits 7b8d58a, 0ac6af3, 9585897): on Linux 6.18 or newer, a memslot update after the irqchip registers on the io bus waits for an SRCU grace period, about 20 ms on AMD hosts.
Upstream-Status: merged upstream (PR 6388)
Drop-When: The fork moves to a Firecracker release that contains PR 6388.
